image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_012_thumb.jpg", "page": "12", "label": "12", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/12"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_013_thumb.jpg", "page": "13", "label": "13", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/13"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_014_thumb.jpg", "page": "14", "label": "14", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/14"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_015_thumb.jpg", "page": "15", "label": "15", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/15"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_016_thumb.jpg", "page": "16", "label": "16", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/16"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_017_thumb.jpg", "page": "17", "label": "17", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/17"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_017-01_thumb.jpg", "page": "18", "label": "[18]", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/18"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839", "series": "JSPPD", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPD6", "documentSeriesTitle": "Letter to the Church and Edward Partridge, 20 March 1839", "editorialPageNumber": "13", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/21225849/21225849-0013.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> to condecending, for the dignifide Characters of the Cald and Chosen of God, according to the purposes of his will from before the foundation of the world.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"1679628152434406197\"><a href=\"#1679628152434406197\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans64\"><span id=\"documenttrans64\">64</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See John 17:24; Ephesians 1:4; and 1 Peter 1:20.</p><hr></div></div></aside> to hold the <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"12251524171456153168\"><a href=\"#12251524171456153168\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4091\" topic=\"x4091\" title=\"Keys\">keys</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Keys\"><p>Authority or knowledge of God given to humankind. In the earliest records, the term keys primarily referred to JS’s authority to unlock the “mysteries of the kingdom.” Early revelations declared that both JS and Oliver Cowdery held the keys to bring forth...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/keys\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside>, of the mistres [mysteries] of those things that have ben kept hid from the foundation untill now,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5899035564842240225\"><a href=\"#5899035564842240225\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans65\"><span id=\"documenttrans65\">65</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See <a href=\"/paper-summary/book-of-mormon-1830/553\" class=\"externalLink\">Book of Mormon, 1830 ed., 547</a> [Ether 4:15].</p><hr></div></div></aside> of which som have tasted a little and which many of them are to be pored down from heaven upon the heads of babes, yea the weak, obscure and dispizable ones of this earth. tharefore We beseath of you bretheren, that <span class=\"josephswriting\">you bear</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"17671859168770845168\"><a href=\"#17671859168770845168\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans8\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Deletion and insertion in the handwriting of JS.</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span>with those who do not feel themselves more worthey than yourselves, while we Exort one another, to a reffermation [reformation], with one an all. both old and young. teachers and taugt both high and low rich and poor—bond and free. Male and female. let honesty and sobriety, and cander and solemnity, and virtue, and pureness, and Meekness, and simplisity, Crown our heads in every place, and in fine becom as little Children<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"8058550215032189417\"><a href=\"#8058550215032189417\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans66\"><span id=\"documenttrans66\">66</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Matthew 18:3.</p><hr></div></div></aside> without mallice guile or Hypokrisy:<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"18369735731060254976\"><a href=\"#18369735731060254976\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans67\"><span id=\"documenttrans67\">67</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See 1 Peter 2:1.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and now Bretheren after your tribulations if you do this— things, and exercise fervent prayer,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6788485788274912275\"><a href=\"#6788485788274912275\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans68\"><span id=\"documenttrans68\">68</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See James 5:16.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and faith in the sight of God Always, he shall give unto you knowledge [p. 13]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> to condecending, for the dignifide Characters <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>of the Cald and Chosen of God, according <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>to the purposes of his <span class=\"deleted\">word</span> will from befo[re] <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>the foundation of the world.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"12667941833396568585\"><a href=\"#12667941833396568585\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans64\"><span id=\"documenttrans64\">64</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See John 17:24; Ephesians 1:4; and 1 Peter 1:20.</p><hr></div></div></aside> to hold the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"9840442988837140914\"><a href=\"#9840442988837140914\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4091\" topic=\"x4091\" title=\"Keys\">keys</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Keys\"><p>Authority or knowledge of God given to humankind. In the earliest records, the term keys primarily referred to JS’s authority to unlock the “mysteries of the kingdom.” Early revelations declared that both JS and Oliver Cowdery held the keys to bring forth...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/keys\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside>, of the mistres [mysteries] of those things that <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>have ben kept hid from the foundation <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>untill now,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10585321198322387039\"><a href=\"#10585321198322387039\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans65\"><span id=\"documenttrans65\">65</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See <a href=\"/paper-summary/book-of-mormon-1830/553\" class=\"externalLink\">Book of Mormon, 1830 ed., 547</a> [Ether 4:15].</p><hr></div></div></aside> <span class=\"deleted\">for</span> &lt;​of​&gt; which som have tasted <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>a little and which many of them are <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>to be pored down from heaven upon the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>heads of babes, yea the weak, obscure <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and dispizable ones of this earth. tharefore <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>We beseath of you bretheren, that <span class=\"deleted\">bare</span> &lt;​<span class=\"josephswriting\">you bear</span>​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6203758990467730308\"><a href=\"#6203758990467730308\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans8\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Deletion and insertion in the handwriting of JS.</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span>with <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>those [w]ho do not feel themselves more worth<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>ey than yourselves, while we Exort one <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>another, to a reffermation [reformation?], with one an <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>all. both old and young. teachers and taugt <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>both high and low rich and poor—bond and <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>free. Male and female. let honesty <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and sobriety, and cander and solemnity, <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and virtue, and pureness, and Meekness, <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and simplisity, Crown our heads in every <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>place, and in fine becom as little Children<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6125190529663432215\"><a href=\"#6125190529663432215\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans66\"><span id=\"documenttrans66\">66</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Matthew 18:3.</p><hr></div></div></aside> <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>without mallice guile or <span class=\"deleted\">high packrichy</span> <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>Hypokrisy:<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13879680817179968951\"><a href=\"#13879680817179968951\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans67\"><span id=\"documenttrans67\">67</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See 1 Peter 2:1.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and now Bretheren after your <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>tribulations if you do this— things, and exercise <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>fervent prayer,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"1882843200773401814\"><a href=\"#1882843200773401814\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans68\"><span id=\"documenttrans68\">68</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See James 5:16.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and faith in the sight of God <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>Always, he shall give unto you knowledge [p. 13]</div></body></html>", "calendarsOfDocuments": [], "versions": [{"versionTitle": "Letter to the Church and Edward Partridge, 20 March 1839", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/1", "versionFeatured": "true"}, {"versionTitle": "Letter to the Church and Edward Partridge, 20 March 1839, as Published in <em xmlns:tei=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" xmlns:lds=\"https://ldsc.xmlref.com/local/ldschurch\">Times and Seasons</em>", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839-as-published-in-times-and-seasons/1", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": " History, 1838–1856, volume C-1 [2 November 1838–31 July 1842]", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/history-1838-1856-volume-c-1-2-november-1838-31-july-1842/81", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "“History of Joseph Smith”", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/history-of-joseph-smith/333", "versionFeatured": ""}], "images": {"smallImageUrl": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_013_thumb.jpg", "mediumImageUrl": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_013_med.jpg", "largeImageUrl": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_013.jpg", "downloadImageUrl": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_013_download.jpg"}, "imageCredit": "", "facsimile": "", "dzUrlXml": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_013.xml", "classification": "Documents", "publishedStatus": "FinalContent", "accessionNumber": "430", "requestedPageNumber": "13", "numberOfPages": "18", "editorialTitle": "Letter to the Church and Edward Partridge, 20 March 1839", "cleanEditorialTitle": "Letter to the Church and Edward Partridge, 20 March 1839", "date": "March 20, 1839", "handwriting": "Ha